{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Evidence from [rebar:2876-7958-8dee-4882] that likely explains some overlap-judge failures.\n\nThe 8 `overlap-judge` failures recorded in `/tmp/03ef-review6.out` were NOT judge-logic failures.\nThey were `status_code: 401 authentication_error` on `model=anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6` — a\nDIRECT-ANTHROPIC call issued by a project configured entirely for Bedrock.\n\nRoot cause (proven on 2876): `overlap/judge.py` binds its model with\n`resolve_model_string(STANDARD_CLASS)` threading no `repo_root`, and the LLM config table was\ndiscovered from the ambient cwd/`REBAR_ROOT` rather than from the gate's pinned code root. When\nambient discovery missed the project's `rebar.toml`, `parse_class_slots({})` returned the\nbuilt-in bare-Anthropic defaults, so the judge called direct Anthropic and 401'd. `judge_one` /\n`judge_batch` swallow ANY exception as an abstain (deliberately — the overlap step is advisory\nand must never fail a review), so the failure surfaced only as \"the judge abstained\", not as a\nprovider misroute.\n\nConsequence for this ticket: overlap-judge failure counts collected BEFORE the fix are\ncontaminated. An unknown share of them are this misroute rather than a judge problem, and\nbecause the failure path is a silent abstain they are indistinguishable in aggregate. Re-measure\nafter change https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1494 lands before drawing conclusions\nabout judge quality."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786102301885959001,"uuid":"f73c2511-eca1-4e6f-83b2-ffe5475ac446"}